<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46281" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suc-cĭno</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subc-</span></b> ; also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">succăno</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 6, § 75</span></i>
		Müll.), ĕre, v. a. and
			n.
		cano, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to sing to</i>, <i>accompany</i> (rare).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tubicines imitatus est succinente
					Habinnā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Petr. 69, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cantibus iste tuis alterno succinet ore,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Calp.
					Ecl. 4, 79</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>, <i>to accord</i>, <i>agree</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">(agricultura) succinit pastorali,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 2, 16</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">clamat: Victum date. Succinit alter: Et mihi,
					etc.,</span>”
				<i>another chimes in</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 17, 48</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
